  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Funds will support veterinary operations to deploy security tracking equipment on Zambias reintroduced population of southern black rhinos and advanced training for anti-poaching staff. Specific activities will 1) include expenses to bring in veterinarians and pilots for a seven day immobilization operation to dart clean (unmarked) rhinos and install VHF transmitters in 5 rhinos and Argos satellite transmitters on two rhinos; 2) ongoing monitoring of rhinos for anti-poaching purposes including operating costs for ground patrols, outposts and 100 hours of aerial surveillance flights; and 3) employing a trainer for advanced training for 15 ZAWA patrol leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
